# Simple Calculator using Verilog

## Description

This project implements a simple calculator using Verilog HDL.

The calculator performs four basic arithmetic operations:

- Addition
- Subtraction
- Multiplication
- Division

## Inputs

- A - 4-bit input
- B - 4-bit input
- Operation - 2-bit operation selector

## Output

- Result - 8-bit calculation result

## Operation Table

| Operation | Function |
|-----------|----------|
| 00 | Addition |
| 01 | Subtraction |
| 10 | Multiplication |
| 11 | Division |

## Example

A = 8
B = 4

8 + 4 = 12
8 - 4 = 4
8 × 4 = 32
8 ÷ 4 = 2

## Tools Used

- Verilog HDL
- Icarus Verilog
- GTKWave
- GitHub

## Files

- `calculator.v` - Calculator design code
- `calculator_tb.v` - Testbench
- `simulation/` - Simulation waveform

## Simulation

Compile:

iverilog -o calculator_sim calculator.v calculator_tb.v

Run:

vvp calculator_sim

View waveform:

gtkwave calculator.vcd

## Result

The simple calculator was successfully designed and simulated using Verilog HDL.